---

## 1. Executive Summary & Vision

### 1.1 Executive Summary
**AI Web Builder (AWB)** is a local-first, open-source, universal website generation platform. It synthesizes architectural patterns from over 46 generative AI website builder experiments into a single cohesive platform. 

Unlike conventional AI code generation tools that emit unstyled snippets or shallow single-file demonstrations, AWB creates **production-grade, 13-layer full-stack software architectures** directly from natural language prompts, starter templates, or live website clones.

### 1.2 Core Pillars
1. **Local-First & Sovereign AI**: Operates 100% offline using local inference runtimes (Ollama, llama.cpp, ComfyUI) with zero telemetry, zero mandatory cloud accounts, and zero subscription lock-in.
2. **13-Layer Architecture**: Generates not merely frontends, but comprehensive systems encompassing UI, API, Database, Authentication, Storage, CI/CD, Deployment, Testing, Security, Rate Limiting, Caching, Load Balancing, and Observability/Recovery.
3. **Dual Delivery Modality**: Distributed both as a lightweight client-side Next.js web application and as a native desktop application (Windows NSIS EXE, macOS DMG, Linux AppImage) powered by Electron.
4. **Provider-Agnostic Engine**: Unified runtime abstraction over 10+ AI providers (local Ollama/llama.cpp and cloud OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, Groq, DeepSeek, Mistral, Together AI, and OpenRouter).
5. **Structural Website Cloning**: Employs an intelligent BFS web crawler to extract architectural layout and typography context from live sites without scraping copyrighted assets.

